# Failing-first tests in tests/fm-project-capacity.test.sh, on upstream-lean: test_freed_tree_goes_to_the_highest_priority_waiter is red because a P1 that waited longer and retries first takes a freed tree from the waiting P0 (agent-config .agent-config-wnvf0: GSP P0 gsp-dc9j6-6 lost two trees on 10-29). test_later_arrival_of_one_priority_waits_behind is red because a later arrival takes the tree. test_same_second_arrivals_keep_their_order is red because a later arrival takes the tree; at this PR's first head d8821a62 it was red too, because ties within one second fell to the task id (chip's review). test_one_task_id_in_two_homes_keeps_two_places and test_two_returned_trees_wake_two_waiters are red because no line exists; at ae7d2f9b they were red too, because a second home's same task id overwrote the first's entry and each returned tree woke the unchanged head (chip's review). test_one_home_keeps_one_place_from_any_checkout and test_two_concurrent_returns_wake_two_waiters are red because no line exists; at da35c20b they were red too, because the home's place followed the caller's git object format and two returners woke the head twice (chip's review). test_wake_never_removes_a_refreshed_waiter is red because no line exists; at 607bb0f6 it was red too, because a wake, which holds no project lock, deleted an entry it had read as gone after a retry refreshed it (chip's review). test_homes_with_one_checksum_keep_two_places is red because no line exists; at b2810ac4 it was red too, because two homes' state paths shared one 32-bit cksum, so each home's leave took the other's place (chip's review). test_one_pool_keeps_one_line_from_any_checkout is red because no line exists; at 4cfffa5b it was red too, because the project lock's identity, and so the line's directory, followed the caller's git object format, so a P1 checking from a SHA-256 checkout saw no P0 ahead of it (chip's review). test_uncounted_pool_keeps_its_line is red because no line exists; at 924c8af1 it was red too, because a project whose pool cannot be counted had no line, so a start passed the waiter ahead of it (chip's review). test_undispatchable_start_holds_no_place is red because no line exists; at 4f36385d it was red too, because that deferral also took a place in the line ahead of a queued P1 (chip's review). test_line_priority_comes_from_the_preflight_read is red because no line exists; at 765134d0 it was red too, because the line re-read the priority and a failed second read left the P0 with none (chip's review). test_claimed_idle_tree_is_never_handed_to_the_allocator and test_claimed_tree_idle_by_steering_is_never_handed_to_the_allocator are red because no line exists; at 765134d0 they were red too, because those deferrals took no place in the line (chip's review). In tests/fm-spawn-defer-slot.test.sh, test_clean_defer_wakes_the_tree_line is red because no line exists; at e2720c5e it was red too, because a deferral after checkout returned its tree through spawn_return_checked_out_ship_slot and woke no waiter (chip's review). In tests/fm-spawn-worktree-settle.test.sh, test_pool_full_herdr_cleanup_is_confirmed (flat closed) is red at 924c8af1 and on upstream-lean, because the allocator's full-pool deferral took no place in a line (chip's review). In tests/fm-secondmate-safety.test.sh, test_secondmate_force_teardown_wakes_a_child_trees_line is red because no line exists; at 924c8af1 it was red too, because the child tree's wake was named after its project's home was removed (chip's review). test_stale_waiter_stops_holding_the_line and test_waiter_lives_as_long_as_its_owner are red because a start deferred on a full pool joins no line. test_teardown_wakes_the_head_waiter_at_once is red because the head starts 3.5-6.9 s after the teardown, at its retry. All are green after this change.
pr: 196
